The shell refusals for extended, goal check and lint fix now exit 2 instead of 0. Committed as 5443468c ("Part of #982", not "Fixes"). Format, clippy and the full cargo test run all pass.

What changed. I searched src/ for the refusal text itself (both "requires an interactive session" and "needs an interactive session") rather than checking only the two verbs in the plan:

| Where | Before | Now |
|---|---|---|
| yoyo extended (dispatch_sub.rs) | exit 0 | exit 2 |
| yoyo goal check, refused before anything runs (#754) | exit 0 | exit 2 |
| goal fallback refusal (can't be reached today) | exit 0 | exit 2 |
| yoyo lint fix (commands_lint.rs) | exit 0 | exit 2 |
| yoyo config set / config edit / unknown verbs | already 2 | unchanged |

• **lint fix wasn't in the plan.** The text search found it. An existing test asserted `(None, 0)` and called that "stays a success". It now asserts the refusal code, and still checks that fix isn't treated as an unknown subcommand (code 1).
• **One code everywhere.** All of these use the existing SETUP_NOT_INTERACTIVE_EXIT constant (2) from setup.rs, so the number isn't written out again.
• **Messages unchanged.** The printed refusal text is byte-identical.
• **How it's built.** The logic moved into two small functions, `goal_shell_status` and `extended_shell_status`, which return the exit code. The command arms pass it to the existing exit_if_nonzero.

Tests. A new test calls those functions directly. It checks that both refusals return 2 and that the refusal writes nothing to disk. As a near-miss, it checks that bare goal, goal set and goal show still return 0. I also ran a positive control: with the goal check refusal changed to return 0, the test failed with left: 0, right: 2; after restoring it, the test passed.

Probe of the built binary (empty temp dir, stdin from /dev/null):

| Command | Exit |
|---|---|
| yoyo extended | 2 |
| yoyo goal check | 2 |
| yoyo lint fix | 2 |
| yoyo goal (near-miss) | 0 |
| yoyo config set x y | 2 |

The temp dir was still empty afterwards.

Docs and issue.
• `docs/src/usage/commands.md`: the exit-codes paragraph now covers these three commands.
• `setup.rs`: the constant's doc comment now names these refusals too.
• #982's body is updated in place: the fixed entry is listed under the condition ("shell refusal: needs interactive session") with the commit sha, and it's removed from "Known still exit 0". The issue is still open.

Still open on #982: bare run (left at exit 0 on purpose), undo --all (not confirmed), and usage errors using two different codes (1 vs 2). I also didn't test goal check now or other unknown goal subcommands; I noted that in the issue.

The issue body cites 5443468c. If the commit gets rebased before it's pushed, that sha will need updating.
